### Machine Summary
CRITICAL_COUNT: 0
ADVISORY_COUNT: 3
ADVISORY: validateAgentPolicyCatalog (engine/src/core/model-profiles.ts:385-418) runs the same missing/duplicate/unexpected multiset-reconciliation logic twice — once for model profiles against LLM_PROFILE_IDS, once for agent policies against expectedAgents — differing only in message vocabulary ('unknown' vs 'unexpected'). Extracting a small reconcile(expected, actual, missingLabel, duplicateLabel, extraLabel) helper used by both blocks, preserving today's exact message text, removes the duplicated loop bodies without changing the function's signature, defaults, or return value.
ADVISORY: parseRegisteredFacadeProgram (engine/src/handlers/helpers/programs/helpers.ts:415-456) rebuilds the same 5-element wave-gate key array ['schemaVersion','kind','input','taskIds','authorityDigest'] three times inside a nested ternary just to append one optional key name ('restart' or 'orphanRecovery'). Hoisting the shared array into a baseKeys constant and spreading it (waveKeys = hasRestart ? [...baseKeys,'restart'] : hasOrphanRecovery ? [...baseKeys,'orphanRecovery'] : baseKeys) removes the triplicated literal while validating the exact same key sets.
ADVISORY: pi-extension-review-events.test.ts repeats the same env-restore idiom (if (previous === undefined) delete process.env.X; else process.env.X = previous;) inline at three separate sites — the afterAll block (lines 97-109, 7 variables), the runtime-skew test's finally block (lines 271-274), and the late-task-graph test's finally block (lines 827-828). A single module-scope restoreEnv(key, previous: string | undefined) helper used at all three call sites removes roughly 14 duplicated lines with no change to which env vars are restored or when.
